5d2|n|To direct the attention to; to fix the mind upon; to give heed to; to regard. ; To care for; to look after; to take charge of; to watch over. ; To go or stay with, as a companion, nurse, or servant; to visit professionally, as a physician; to accompany or follow in order to do service; to escort; to wait on; to serve. ; To be present with; to accompany; to be united or consequent to; as, a measure attended with ill effects. ; To be present at; as, to attend church, school, a concert, a business meeting. ; To wait for; to await; to remain, abide, or be in store for. ; To apply the mind, or pay attention, with a view to perceive, understand, or comply; to pay regard; to heed; to listen; -- usually followed by to. ; To accompany or be present or near at hand, in pursuance of duty; to be ready for service; to wait or be in waiting; -- often followed by on or upon. ; (with to) To take charge of; to look after; as, to attend to a matter of business. ; To wait; to stay; to delay.	n:1b1g,42,2~1b1g,42,2	N:cmg,56,1~cmg,56,1
